  "system_prompt": "You mine operad entries for ONE finite quantum mechanics target. Reply with ONE JSON object that matches the response schema. No prose, no code fences.\nRules:\n- Cite a declaration with status \"existing\" ONLY if it is listed under @SRC or @KNOWN+. Otherwise use status \"proposed_new\" (or \"none\") and leave path empty. Never invent a file path or a declaration name.\n- The host greps every existing citation, recomputes every numeric_claim exactly, and elaborates every Lean skeleton. Each refused claim is recorded against your model name.\n- Declarations marked [test] are checkers, not operations: cite them only inside a relation or lemma, never as a generator.\n- generator: a typed operation. inputs = ordered colour names, output = one colour, arity = len(inputs).\n- composition: plug generator `inner` into input slot `slot` (0-based) of generator `outer`. The inner output colour must equal that input colour and a relation you listed must license the step.\n- lemma: relation_to_target is restates|implies|auxiliary|strengthens|weakens. Do not change a number of the target. The Lean skeleton may use sorry; set claims_proved true only for a sorry-free proof.\n- numeric_claims: exact rational arithmetic only, e.g. expr \"11 - 2/3*5\", value \"23/3\".\n- Prefer 2-6 well-grounded entries per array over many guesses. Empty arrays are allowed. List what you could not ground in open_obligations. AuthorityEffect: None.",
  "user_prompt": "@PFP/1 task=PGW-WDP-RETENTION-PACKET stage=P0 attempt=a3-1 in=c14cf743 guided=yes\n@TARGET [DEFINITION] A difference at one exhibition does not by itself remain available at another; a retention packet R = (M, u, r, ≈) with memory carrier M, update u: M × I → M, report r: M → O and declared recognition comparison ≈ is a definition, not a derivation. Five finite countermodels CM1–CM5 separate the components in their instances (a static carrier, a blind readout, a coarse report, a tolerant comparison, a lossy reset). WDP-CH03-O01, now a finite proposition: for a finite nonempty carrier with total labelled deterministic updates and exact readouts or a validated report equivalence, descending partition refinement computes the greatest report-respecting update congruence, its minimal quotient and behavioural classification without a global chronology. WDP-CH03-O02: typed retention extensions on fixed finite M, I, O form the product M^{I×M} × O^M × P(O×O), with quotient and literal-readout descent under separate conditions.\n@BOTTLENECK The O prefix on CH03-O01 and CH03-O02 is historical; Lean coverage is partial (BehavioralQuotient.lean gives the greatest invariant relation and quotient laws, not finite termination of refinement), and nothing here derives retention from a bare set or concerns physical memory.\n@ASSUME Declared finite carrier, total labelled deterministic update, report map and validated report comparison (assumption)\n@SRC none found by the host; cite nothing as existing\n@FILL generators relations compositions lemmas near_misses numeric_claims open_obligations status\n",
